ction. Thoroughly cleans every mess,” and On-screen text at the bottom reads, “Robot Vacuum) I’ll clean up the floors, so you two can enjoy a little alone time” along with a disclaimer stating, “Able to use 10W suction power at Spot Mode with Vacuum Only, and can last up to 60 min. Based on testing result of Korea Testing Laboratory (KTL), in accordance with KS B 7303:2025 5.1.7. Max suction power was measured with empty dustbin and fully charged battery. Actual results may vary depending on environmental factors.” The scene cuts to the Bespoke AI Laundry Combo automatically opening its door with the text, “Auto Open Door+. Opens to let air out when cycle ends,” along with disclaimers stating, “Auto Open Door+ automatically opens the door and blows air to help remove moisture inside the drum more quickly. The default setting for Auto Open Door is \u0027Open 5 mins later\u0027 after a wash-only cycle, and \u0027Open immediately\u0027 after a wash \u0026 dry cycle or dry-only cycle,” and “Auto Open Door+\u0027s airflow operates only after a wash-only cycle is completed. The default setting for the airflow is Off, and this can be changed in Settings \u003e Washer \u003e Auto Open Door.” Then it cuts to the couple having dinner at the table quickly followed by additional cuts of the Bespoke AI home appliances in use, and On-screen text at the bottom reads, “Fridge) And so, they grow closer, understanding each other more,” and “Fridge) With a little help from our peacemaker AIs.” The scene transitions to a single shot of the Bespoke AI Jet Bot Steam Ultra cleaning the floor with the text “Secured by Knox. 3-layer security solution powered by knox,” and On-screen text at the bottom reads, “Robot Vacuum) No worries, your privacy is fully protected!” along with disclaimers stating, “Knox Vault : On device data protection with a built-in security chip,” “Knox Matrix : Security monitoring across samsung devices,” “Verified with the highest Diamond level in the IoT Security Rating by UL Solutions,” “Certified with the highest Standard Plus level in the IoT Cybersecurity by the Korea Internet \u0026 Security Agency (KISA),” “Certified by TUV Nord, in compliance with ETSI EN 303 645, Cyber Security for Consumer Internet of Things: Baseline Requirements. Obtained the internationally recognized cybersecurity ETSI EN 303 645 Conformity Mark,” “Received the IT Security label from BSI(Bundesamt fur Sicherheit in der Informationstechnik), which is Federal Office for Information Security of Germany.” In the final scene, the Bespoke AI Jet Bot Steam Ultra slides away from the frame and the video closes with the texts, “Enabling Better Living,” following with, “Bespoke AI,” and finally with the Samsung logo.","thumbnailUrl":"https://images.samsung.com/is/image/samsung/assets/pk/offer/26_sw_1h_f04_03_ft11_aimomentfilm_da_720x405.jpg","contentUrl":"https://youtu.be/GIMuv7XOXRE","inLanguage":"en-PK","publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Samsung","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.samsung.com/etc.clientlibs/samsung/clientlibs/consumer/global/clientlib-common/resources/images/logo-square-letter.png"},"@id":"https://www.samsung.com/pk/#org"}}</script>

				
			
				
					
						<div class="video" data-image-default="false" data-video-embed="false" data-video-type="youtube" data-video-data='{
							"id": "Ay0oNREaVuo",
							"title": "A cinematic Samsung showcase introduces AI-powered home living, where connected appliances intuitively understand users to create a seamless, effortless everyday experience.",
							"caption": "A sequence of modern home interiors filled with Samsung appliances appears in quick cuts, showcasing various living spaces styled with connected devices. The scene then shifts to a white laboratory, where researchers are studying and developing home appliances. The products transform into detailed cross-sectional views, revealing their electronic components and engineering structures. These elements transition into visuals of appliances seamlessly connected throughout a home environment. Close-up shots of researchers’ hands and mouths are intercut with abstract scientific imagery, suggesting innovation and communication. The scene then transitions to a close-up of a human eye, followed by real-life home settings where the appliances are actively in use. A happy couple, a relaxed child, and a dog are shown enjoying a comfortable home environment. People continue interacting with different appliances across various scenes, highlighting ease and convenience. Various appliances are featured, including a washer, refrigerator, robot vacuum, and oven—representing Samsung’s home appliance lineup. In the next shot, a woman places food into a refrigerator, and the item is identified by AI as a bell pepper. In the final shot, multiple Samsung appliances are neatly aligned in a row. In front of them, the text “Your Companion to AI Living” appears. The video concludes with the Samsung logo.",
							"autoplay": false}'>
						</div>
					
					
					
					
						
					
